    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently mini.files shows the directory names and file names. There is no option given in config that will let user know how many files (directories are present inside any directory. So if there will be an option that will enable the support for showing files/directory count inside any directory. First directory name will be shown then count of files inside that directory. \neg. \ndirectory_name    (12)",
