    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI think this is a bit too much (what I consider not *quite* useful) info to show near every file system entry. It will also add performance penalty, and probably significant (because it has to traverse each directory shown in *current* window).\n\nIn this form this is not planned. The alternatives are:\n- Use `config.content.prefix` to show this information. It will require handling the alignment and will be highlighted in the same way as an icon, but feels like a reasonable compromise. Here is the quick example of how I'd do it:\n\n    ```lua\n    local prefix = function(fs_entry)\n      local icon, hl = MiniFiles.default_prefix(fs_entry)\n      if fs_entry.fs_type == 'directory' then\n        local n_inside = #vim.fn.readdir(fs_entry.path)\n        icon = string.format('%s(%03d) ', icon, n_inside)\n      end\n      return icon, hl\n    end\n    require('mini.files').setup({ content = { prefix = prefix } })\n    ```\n\n    And here is how it looks:\n\n    <img width=\"2880\" height=\"1734\" alt=\"screenshot_2026-11-17_16:35:23\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f50161e1-f7a0-43c6-b436-bf08c8539f66\" />\n\n- Modify borders to show the number of files and directories *in the current window* as footer. Then the number of entries in the directory at cursor can be viewed if preview is enabled. This is something that probably will be added in the future natively and by default.",
            "created_at": "2026-11-17T14:41:08Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2601#issuecomment-6951256148",
